<section class="homepage-overview">
    <div class="overview-copy">
        <span class="sec-lbl">What it solves</span>
        <h2 class="serif">A complete booking workspace for both sides of the event</h2>
        <p>Most small and mid-sized events still manage stalls through phone calls, scattered forms, screenshots, and manual payment checks. StallBazar brings those steps into one role-based system that is easy to explain, easy to demo, and useful for real organizers.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="overview-grid">
        <article><strong>01</strong><h3>Publish events</h3><p>Organizers add venue, category, event dates, event photos, map images, stall prices, and stall availability.</p></article>
        <article><strong>02</strong><h3>Request stalls</h3><p>Vendors compare options, choose a stall, add a note, and send a booking request through their account.</p></article>
        <article><strong>03</strong><h3>Review payments</h3><p>Payment references and approval status stay attached to the booking, so organizers can verify before confirming.</p></article>
        <article><strong>04</strong><h3>Track updates</h3><p>Dashboards and notifications show what is pending, approved, rejected, booked, or still available.</p></article>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="swap-section thinking">
    <div class="section-intro">
        <span>The StallBazar advantage</span>
        <h2 class="serif">A booking flow that handles the actual handoffs</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="benefit-loop">
        <article><h3>Discover the right event</h3><p>Vendors browse active events, categories, locations, dates, and stall availability before sending a request.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Pick from a visual map</h3><p>Layouts make availability clear, so vendors understand position, size, zone, and price before booking.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Approve without conflict</h3><p>Organizers review requests, confirm deposits, and avoid accidental double bookings from one dashboard.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Track the full journey</h3><p>Notifications and role dashboards keep everyone aligned from request to approval to event day.</p></article>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="kpi-band">
    <div class="kpi-copy">
        <span>Trust by design</span>
        <h2 class="serif">Clear rules instead of unsupported marketplace claims</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-grid">
        <article><strong>01</strong><span>Organizer-owned event records</span></article>
        <article><strong>02</strong><span>Terms visible before applying</span></article>
        <article><strong>03</strong><span>Deposit status attached to booking</span></article>
        <article><strong>04</strong><span>Protected stall allocation</span></article>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="quote-rail">
    <article><div class="quote-logo">Transparent listing</div><h3>Dates, audience, facilities, vendor rules, prices, and cancellation terms belong in one place.</h3><p>Vendors should not need private messages to understand the basic commercial terms of an event.</p></article>
    <article><div class="quote-logo">Accountable organizer</div><h3>Every event is tied to the organizer who owns and manages its stalls.</h3><p>Public contact details and organizer profile information give vendors a clear channel for questions.</p></article>
    <article><div class="quote-logo">Auditable booking</div><h3>Requests, deposit references, decisions, and notifications stay connected.</h3><p>Both sides can see the current state instead of relying on scattered calls and screenshots.</p></article>
</section>

<section class="role-showcase">
    <div class="section-intro wide">
        <span>Role-based dashboards</span>
        <h2 class="serif">Different users see the tools they actually need</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="role-showcase-grid">
        <article>
            <div class="role-tag">Vendors</div>
            <h3>Find and request a stall</h3>
            <p>Browse public events, review maps, check pricing, submit stall requests, add deposit references, and see booking status from the vendor dashboard.</p>
            <ul><li>Search events by category and venue</li><li>Compare stall size, tier, zone, and price</li><li>Track pending and approved bookings</li></ul>
        </article>
        <article>
            <div class="role-tag">Organizers</div>
            <h3>Publish and approve with control</h3>
            <p>Create event pages, upload venue visuals, configure stall layouts, review vendor notes, verify payments, and prevent double booking.</p>
            <ul><li>Create events and stall inventory</li><li>Approve or reject requests</li><li>Keep vendors updated through notifications</li></ul>
        </article>
        <article>
            <div class="role-tag">Admin</div>
            <h3>Monitor platform activity</h3>
            <p>Admins can review platform totals, events, bookings, and user activity so the whole system remains easier to supervise.</p>
            <ul><li>View dashboard metrics</li><li>Monitor event and booking activity</li><li>Support users across roles</li></ul>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="swap-section platform">
    <div class="section-intro wide">
        <span>Event commerce platform</span>
        <h2 class="serif">A living stall marketplace, not a static listing page</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="platform-grid">
        <article class="platform-card"><div><span>01</span><h3>Discovery becomes guided browsing</h3><p>Events are presented by category, venue, date, and availability so vendors can quickly find the best match.</p><a asp-controller="Events" asp-action="Index">Explore events</a></div><div class="visual-card visual-one"></div></article>
        <article class="platform-card"><div><span>02</span><h3>Stall choice becomes visual</h3><p>Interactive maps turn abstract stall numbers into clear zones, dimensions, tiers, and booking states.</p><a asp-controller="Events" asp-action="Index">View layouts</a></div><div class="visual-card visual-two"></div></article>
        <article class="platform-card"><div><span>03</span><h3>Approvals happen in the flow</h3><p>Organizers can move from review to confirmation while vendors stay informed through their dashboard.</p><a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Login">Sign in</a></div><div class="visual-card visual-three"></div></article>
        <article class="platform-card"><div><span>04</span><h3>Event day stays organized</h3><p>Final stall assignments, request status, and vendor records remain easy to scan when the venue gets busy.</p><a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Register">Start booking</a></div><div class="visual-card visual-four"></div></article>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="story-grid">
    <article class="story-card large"><div class="story-image story-one"></div><div><span>Food festival</span><h3 class="serif">Premium entrance stalls booked without back-and-forth calls</h3><p>Organizers can publish the map once and let vendors request available spaces directly.</p></div></article>
    <article class="story-card"><div class="story-image story-two"></div><div><span>Trade expo</span><h3 class="serif">Clear zones for sponsors, exhibitors, and service areas</h3></div></article>
    <article class="story-card"><div class="story-image story-three"></div><div><span>Community bazaar</span><h3 class="serif">Local vendors get a simpler way to join events</h3></div></article>
